ary this isn't going away and maybe  it's going away for the short term but  it's not going away for the catering  business for a while and our business is  is change for six months to a year for  the foreseeable future so we need to  adapt we need a pivot and that's what  we've done it's tough to turn on a dime  but you have to it's survival of the  fittest and so you do what you have to  do and you just do it and we've done it  my name is Aziz Alam ko owner at good  neighbor it's a mini department store we  call it it's more than clothing we do or  footwear we do a lot of lifestyle  anything that relates to a young family  and their kids pre coalbed we were doing  incredible we're doing very well we were  very busy we took on a big expansion  plan for the store a second floor we  didn't know the severity of it until it  hit us and we right away figured out we  have this little website that we had pre  kovat it's a brick and mortar business  it was never gonna be an online business  but online has exposed us in a different  way now it's all organic to mean a  bidder all the government support that  we got thank God we were able to hold on  to some of our staff and they were they  were key in this thing they all rallied  around the business and they helped us  out to on personally to fill the store  the online store the doors are closed  but really were still open  I personally really engaged with these  people I know them all very well so I  decided to take on the whole delivery of  the local area myself I started knocking  the door leaving a box running out of  there with my mask on and it turned out  that everybody everybody started coming  out of the doors and saying hello to me  and that was that was amazing it's a  lifeline right now it's only it's a like  I said it's a drop in the bucket for  what it needs to happen the most  important thing that could have happened  is because it is keeping us in engaged  with our actual consumer who shops here  good morning